{"command":"record_issue_mutation","content":{"intent_digest":"9bcd781bf7fce3e4e4ffb5f8f98c8a112b4a1d6d27fce63386f9ed35aff809c6","operation_digest":"dfb904d722c078f97b1ea1182ddc99244d069749691712b1f3536c9dda0fbdcd","request":{"credential_names":["GITHUB_TOKEN"],"cutover_issue":null,"expected_head_sha":"f69019c24a9b61511e912c93f95442f96fa66d92","issue":978,"mutation":{"action":"issue_edit","body":"## Problem\n\nThe live frontier-provider rollout exposed three coupled restart hazards after Sprint 2 provider work merged:\n\n1. `csm runtime-v3 start` can successfully bootstrap the launchd job but leave it loaded and never started (`runs = 0`) until an operator manually invokes `launchctl kickstart`.\n2. A syntactically valid complete-map `providers.yaml` can omit a provider referenced by resident or persisted dynamic agents. Candidate admission succeeds, activation advances, and the kernel then exits while loading agent state, taking down the control plane.\n3. Hosted API keys currently reach the service only through transient launchd environment values. A later crash or managed restart loses them even though the approved key files still exist.\n\nThese are operational defects found while configuring the frontier models after #855 and #967. Preserve the prior issue and PR histories.\n\n## Required outcome\n\nMake the ordinary managed start path self-contained and fail-soft. Starting Runtime must launch the exact managed service, invalid provider replacement state must not make the control plane unavailable, and hosted credentials must survive managed restarts through credential-file references without storing secret values in repository files, plist files, logs, or command arguments.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] On macOS, canonical `csm runtime-v3 start` drives an unloaded or loaded-but-idle launchd service into execution and readiness without manual `launchctl` commands.\n- [ ] Focused service-manager tests cover bootstrap plus kickstart, already-running idempotence, command failure, and timeout behavior.\n- [ ] Initial and hot-reload provider candidates are checked against resident and persisted dynamic agent bindings before promotion, or otherwise retain the last-known-good registry while Runtime remains available with a redacted diagnostic.\n- [ ] Removing a referenced provider cannot advance the active provider generation or terminate Runtime.\n- [ ] Malformed provider state still fails closed without weakening TLS, signed A2A, replay, capability, or continuity checks.\n- [ ] OpenAI and Anthropic adapters accept governed credential-file references; the service reads the files at dispatch time or startup without exposing their contents.\n- [ ] Managed restart proof shows the hosted provider definitions remain dispatch-ready without transient secret environment values. No paid provider call is required.\n- [ ] Existing environment-variable credential references remain compatible.\n- [ ] Obsolete Runtime config-generation receipt gates are not restored. C-SDLC lifecycle receipts remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Focused deterministic tests, a real local managed-service restart proof, exact-head independent review, and required CI pass.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `adl/src/cli/csm_runtime_v3_cmd.rs`\n- `adl-provider-core/**`\n- `adl-runtime-kernel/**`\n- Runtime v3 service configuration and focused operator documentation/tests\n- Issue-local C-SDLC cards and proof metadata\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Paid model qualification.\n- Removing lifecycle authority, TLS, signed control, replay, or audit evidence.\n- Rewriting #855, #967, or their merged evidence.\n- Broad cleanup of inactive files that did not cause the failure.\n\nFollow-up to #855 and #967. Part of v0.92.2 Sprint 2 corrective reconciliation.\n\n<!-- csdlc-v3-operation:8b4637661c1ba4bb69976f1fcdcb3d50a086c70f582e6db24b660a5d67cfbdab -->\n\n## Additional native bootstrap defect\n\nThe issue-scoped native create receipt for newly assigned #978 was immediately classified as legacy residue, causing `csdlc prepare 978` to refuse the issue with `LegacyMigrationRequired`. Preserve the authenticated creation receipt; preparation must ignore repository-scoped issue-create results when testing issue-local legacy lifecycle residue. Add a regression proving a freshly created issue can be prepared without receipt deletion or manual state repair.\n","title":null},"operator_approval":null,"pull_request":null,"recovery":null,"repository":"agent-logic/agent-design-language"},"schema":"csdlc.v3.staged_github_mutation.v1"},"native":{"identity":"9bcd781bf7fce3e4e4ffb5f8f98c8a112b4a1d6d27fce63386f9ed35aff809c6","owner":"csdlc-v3-github"},"origin":{"binding":{"branch":"codex/978-runtime-startup-provider-resilience","head":"f69019c24a9b61511e912c93f95442f96fa66d92","registration":"f52657a74fb3a42e877b47a489ca783b2fe3eb1972124cd87246fc2ebf0d7d4e","worktree":"/Volumes/FastWork/adl-worktrees/adl-issue-978-runtime-startup-provider-resilience"},"kind":"bound"}}